---

The programs the page compiles, and the payload it ships, embed Crystal's runtime
and standard library, which are Apache-2.0:

- Crystal compiler and standard library: Apache-2.0
- wasi-libc (linked into every program): MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
- PCRE2 (linked in when a program uses `Regex`): BSD-3-Clause
- LLVM (linked into the compiler, and into the linker the page runs): Apache-2.0
  WITH LLVM-exception

The toolchain that produces them lives in `build/crystal-wasm/` — patched sources and
scripts, not redistributed here: Crystal 1.17.0 from the official distribution, wasi-sdk 33
for `wasm-ld` and the WASI sysroot, and PCRE2 built from source for wasm. The libLLVM the
compiler links against is built by the
[`llvm-wasm`](https://github.com/live-codes/llvm-wasm) repository. The one third-party
component vendored into the package is `@bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim`, under
`packages/crystal-wasm/vendor/` with its own licence files; the package's
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is the authoritative list of what it ships.
